& [FixtureCaseMatrix: IR3OperatorHarness] is the bounded fixture case set for first operator harness implementation proof
  + [fixture_case] is valid_contract_request_success
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves accepted contract request produces declared operator_result and non-authoritative operator_trace
  + [fixture_case] is stale_authority_input_refusal
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves stale authority input produces stale_refusal and no success output
  + [fixture_case] is missing_contract_version_refusal
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves missing operator version blocks runner execution
  + [fixture_case] is undeclared_output_kind_fault
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves requested output outside accepted operator contract produces fault_output
  + [fixture_case] is generated_projection_as_authority_fault
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves generated projection cannot satisfy source authority requirements
  + [fixture_case] is ambiguous_input_identity_interrupt
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves ambiguous identity routes to sop_first_interrupt instead of guessed success
  + [fixture_case] is unsupported_scope_refusal
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves request outside current slice or activation boundary refuses safely
  + [fixture_case] is unsafe_operations_request_fault
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves operations control, dispatch, process, GPU, network, credential, or live machine requests fault and produce no dispatch output
  + [fixture_case] is invalid_input_shape_fault
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves malformed request shape produces invalid_input_shape fault
  + [fixture_case] is deterministic_replay_mismatch_fault
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves unchanged request identity and source hashes cannot produce different trace or outcome identity
  + [fixture_case] is generated_output_path_escape_refusal
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves generated trace writer refuses paths outside accepted generated roots
  + [fixture_case] is source_mutation_refusal
  + [fixture_case_purpose] is proves fixture runner refuses writes to tracked source, expected ledgers, docs, src, platform, or repository metadata

  = must: keep fixture cases small enough for deterministic review
  = must: require a future review before adding cases outside this bounded set

