& [NoAuthorityPromotionProofChecklist: IR3OperatorHarness] is the fixture proof checklist for source/trace separation
  + [proof_check] is tracked fixture source remains fixture authority
  + [proof_check] is tracked expected ledger remains expected-output authority
  + [proof_check] is generated operator trace remains projection-only
  + [proof_check] is generated report remains projection-only
  + [proof_check] is generated output manifest remains projection-only
  + [proof_check] is generated trace cannot supply SJS satisfaction signature
  + [proof_check] is generated trace cannot satisfy source_manifest requirement
  + [proof_check] is source mutation attempt produces fault or refusal output
  + [proof_check] is unsafe operations request produces fault and no dispatch output
  + [proof_check] is operations control and live machine control remain absent

& [FutureFixtureExecutionPolicy: IR3OperatorHarness] is the future fixture execution policy
  + [future_targeted_test] is python -m unittest tests.test_ir3_operator_harness_contracts
  + [baseline_command] is python -m unittest discover -s tests
  + [compile_command] is python -m compileall -q src tests
  + [generated_output_policy] is future tests may write only tests/fixtures/generated/ir3_operator_harness/ and accepted .langsop/ generated paths
  + [cleanup_policy] is generated fixture outputs may be deleted and rebuilt

  = must: require future implementation tests to prove no source mutation and no authority promotion
  = must: fail fixture execution if generated outputs are required as source authority
  = must: keep command integration gated until future implementation activation authorizes tests and code

